This was my first tourist ascension.  It was actually much easier than I
expected (or maybe I just got lucky); I found it much easier and fun than
my previous ranger ascension <brag>which was also my previous game!</brag>.

I used a number of different weapon combinations in this game:
- bare handed combat + darts in the very early game
- graduated to a short sword when I found one
- two-weaponed what turned out to be a +0 elvish short sword and +1
  dwarvish short sword
- got Were-bane from #offering, practiced with this, and then two-weaponed
  with one of the short swords
- found Magicbane in a bones pile; picked up a silver saber from a watchfoo
  and two-weaponed these for the rest of the game.  It was a pretty nice
  combination, with Magicbane provided some nice effects (I got it to +3
  instead of +2, didn't bother to pull it back down), and the saber
  providing some extra oomph.

I was a long time acquiring MR and reflection.  I got to xplevel 14 fairly
quickly, thanks to a 2 level bump from a polytrap, a wraith, and a
succubus.  I actually started the quest with no MR or reflection, but I sat
on the throne by the quest leader, which gave me a wish (+3 GDSM).  I
didn't get reflection until I found the castle wand ("oReflection, cloak of
displacement, gauntlets of dex (I already had gauntlets of power, but I'd
been eating lots of giants)).

I cornered my first pet on a polytrap; unfortunately he eventually became
an arch-lich.  I used him to do in most of the shopkeepers, but eventually
I genocided him.  

My next pet, after some polymorphing, became a Titan.  I tried to keep him
around; gave him Frost Brand and a shield of reflection, and geno'd purple
worms.  Somewhere in Gehennom a poly trap got him, but I cornered him there
and it was not too long before he became a Titan again, this time female.
I used the intermediate time to charge up Frost Brand to +5.

Unfortunately somewhere in Gehennom she simply vanished in the time it took
me to distance-move between stairs on a previously dug out level, and I
never saw her again.  Oh well.

Some tense moments on Astral this time, when I foolishly decided to eat a
lembas wafer with Pestilence in the vicinity (I was embarking on the Famine
altar, but Pestilence decided to pop in for a visit).  I was frozen there,
with Pestilence making me sicker and sicker.  Fortunately I came around
before dying, and had enough power for some "cure sickness" spells; it took
me about 5 of these and some unihorn applications to remove the stunning
before I got out of there.  

Once my angel bit it, I donned a ring of conflict, and used some /oTeleport
to clear a path.  The correct altar was the second one I tried (Death).

PYEC rocks!

bclewis, neutral male human Tourist




